# ─── What EAS Build uploads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# EAS packs the whole git root, not just the Expo app, and it reads this file
# *instead of* .gitignore when it does. So every path that must stay out has to be
# named here — including the ones .gitignore already covers, which is the important
# half: the Android signing keystore and its cleartext passwords sit untracked in
# mobile/, and .gitignore is the only reason they are not in every build tarball
# today. That reason does not carry over to this file.
#
# Written as an explicit deny of all 37 root entries except `mobile`, rather than as
# an allow-list, because the uploader prunes excluded directories and does not honour
# `!` re-includes — `/*` plus `!/mobile/` packs a derisory 80-byte archive. Every
# entry below was taken from a listing of the root; a new sibling directory will need
# a line adding, and until it gets one it only costs upload size.
#
# The scope is also simply correct. `mobile/` is a standalone project — no workspace
# root, no shared node_modules — so the .NET API, the Python worker, web-admin and
# docs/ have never been anything but dead weight in an Android build.
#
# Excluding server/ is what gets the build past `server/.pytest-tmp`, a pytest
# basetemp whose ACL denies read to its own owner and which the uploader's directory
# walk therefore hits as an EPERM rather than a skip. The walk does not consult
# .gitignore, so ignoring it there was not enough (it belongs in both).

# ── The other tiers, and the tooling around them ──
/.claude/
/.git/
/.github/
/.preview/
/.vercel/
/.vs/
/docs/
/server/
/spike/
/src/
/tests/
/tools/
/web-admin/
/web-site/

# ── Root files. None of them build an Android app; .env.local and the deploy
#    scripts are the ones that would actually hurt. ──
/.dockerignore
/.easignore
/.editorconfig
/.env.local
/.gitattributes
/.gitignore
/.vercelignore
/AGENTS.md
/Aptfile
/BACKLOG.md
/CLAUDE.md
/Directory.Build.props
/Dockerfile
/NoteFusion.slnx
/Procfile
/README.md
/compose-build-transcriber.log
/compose-up.log
/deploy-heroku.ps1
/deploy-procfile.ps1
/docker-compose.yml
/expo-start.log
/heroku.yml
/launch-pgadmin-fixed.bat

# ── Inside the app: installed, generated, or secret ──
# EAS installs dependencies on the builder.
/mobile/node_modules/
/mobile/.expo/
/mobile/dist/
/mobile/web-build/
# Store-listing renders: megabytes of PNG and video that ship with the *listing*.
/mobile/store/out/
# Signing and publishing material. Remote credentials mean the builder already has
# what it needs from EAS servers; none of this has any business in the tarball.
/mobile/*.jks
/mobile/credentials/
/mobile/credentials.json
/mobile/upload_certificate.pem
/mobile/google-play-service-account.json
/mobile/.env*
